      en: "Wädenswil is located on Lake Zurich in the canton of Zurich and is famous for its wine-growing tradition and scenic setting. The city has a long history of fruit and wine cultivation dating back to the Middle Ages. Today, Wädenswil is a key center for agricultural research, notably through the Agroscope research institute and the Zurich University of Applied Sciences (ZHAW), which maintains a campus here. Viticulture shapes the cityscape with numerous vineyards and wineries. Wädenswil boasts a well-preserved old town with half-timbered houses and a notable Reformed church. The population is around 25,000, and the city is a popular residential area for commuters to Zurich.",
