      en: "Kreuzlingen is located in the canton of Thurgau on Lake Constance and is the second largest city in the canton. It borders directly on the German city of Konstanz, with which it has a close economic and cultural connection. Kreuzlingen is an important transport hub with a port and a railway station on the Zurich–Munich line. The city has a long history as a border town and was a center of the textile industry in the 19th century. Today, the economy is characterized by services, trade, and tourism. The old town of Kreuzlingen is marked by historic buildings such as the Church of St. Ulrich. The population is around 22,000. The city offers numerous leisure opportunities on the lake.",
