      en: "Davos is located in the canton of Graubünden and is a world-renowned holiday resort and conference venue. The town is famous for the World Economic Forum (WEF), held annually in January. Davos consists of two parts: Davos-Dorf and Davos-Platz. The landscape is characterized by the mountains of the Albula and Silvretta Alps. Tourism is the most important economic factor, with skiing in winter and hiking in summer. Davos has a long history as a health resort in the 19th century. The population is around 11,000. The town is served by the Landquart–Davos railway line.",
