      en: "Le Locle is a city in the canton of Neuchâtel, located in the Neuchâtel Jura at 946 m elevation. It is a historic center of Swiss watchmaking, home to companies such as Tissot, Ulysse Nardin, and Zenith. In 2009, Le Locle and nearby La Chaux-de-Fonds were jointly inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site for their outstanding urban planning reflecting the watchmaking culture. The city's population is around 10,000. The watch industry started in the 17th century and remains dominant. Key attractions include the Musée d'Horlogerie (Watch Museum) and the Galerie d'Art. The city's economy is heavily dependent on luxury watches and microtechnology.",
